---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Code from "../../components/docs/Code.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/docs/Callout.astro";
import Endpoint from "../../components/docs/Endpoint.astro";
import Params from "../../components/docs/Params.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Inbound calls" lead="Have one of your agents answer a phone number. Inbound calls run the same pipeline as outbound ones and produce the same events, transcript and log." slug="inbound">
        <h2 id="how">How it works</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Assign a number to an agent with <code>POST /v1/phone-numbers</code>.</li>
          <li>At your carrier, set that number's <strong>answer URL</strong> to <code>https://&lt;your-host&gt;/v1/telephony/inbound</code>.</li>
          <li>When someone calls, Offhook checks the carrier's signature, finds the agent for the dialed number, and connects the call.</li>
        </ol>
        <Callout kind="note">
          The answer URL is called by the carrier, not by you. It is authenticated by the
          carrier's signature and doesn't use an API key.
        </Callout>

        <h2 id="map">Assign a number</h2>
        <Endpoint method="POST" path="/v1/phone-numbers" />
        <Params rows={[
          { name: "e164", type: "string", required: true, desc: "The number in E.164 format, e.g. <code>+14155550123</code>." },
          { name: "agent_id", type: "uuid", required: true, desc: "The agent that answers calls to this number. It needs a telephony connection for the same carrier." },
        ]} />
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "cURL", lang: "bash", code: `curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/v1/phone-numbers \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $OFFHOOK_KEY" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{ "e164": "+14155550123", "agent_id": "<agent-id>" }'` }, { label: "Response", lang: "json", code: `{
  "id": "9d3c7e1a-4f2b-4d8e-b5a9-1c6e3f8d2a70",
  "e164": "+14155550123",
  "agent_id": "3b9e2a7c-1d4f-4e8a-b6c2-5f7a9d1e3c40",
  "created_at": "2026-10-15T10:00:00Z"
}` }]} />
        <p>A number can belong to only one agent. Assigning a number that's already taken returns <code>409</code>.</p>

        <h2 id="manage">List and delete</h2>
        <Endpoint method="GET" path="/v1/phone-numbers" />
        <Endpoint method="DELETE" path="/v1/phone-numbers/{id}" />
        <p>
          Inbound calls appear in your call list with <code>"direction": "inbound"</code>, and
          each one sends a <a href="/docs/webhooks/#events"><code>call.received</code></a> event
          when it arrives.
        </p>

</DocsLayout>
